  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A capacitor of capacitance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> is charged completely using a de supply of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. It is now connected to an inductor of inductance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mH</mi></math> to form an LC circuit. The maximum current in LC circuit will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "10",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Energy stored in capacitor</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mn>500</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p><p>Current will be maximum when whole energy of capacitor becomes energy of inductor.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>L</mi><msup><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
